Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 47/47] Name flushed pieces the phone's upload store holds

With hello 0x8000 (docs/gpu-live.md, "Upload cache") a process asks once per
executor for the store's key prefixes and its allowance (UPLOAD_INVENTORY),
before its first flush of a range of at least 16 KiB. Each whole 4096 bytes of
such a range, counted from its offset, goes as its prefix when the process
knows it, as its bytes for the phone to store while the allowance lasts, and
otherwise through the changed-block shadow as before; pieces leave their bytes
known to the shadow. The decisions, the per-stream known set and the wire forms
are ../bounded-memory/upload_cache.h; chunks of such ranges start at whole
pieces, and a stored piece's key is the BLAKE3 of the copy written.

